{# Run summary table - 3.1.

   One row per checkpoint across the whole run, so a reader can see the shape
   of the run without working through every section. 3.1 fixes the row and
   leaves the columns open; these are the two verdicts that 3.2 refuses to
   collapse, how much of the evidence arrived, what the sensor reported, and
   how many findings named the checkpoint.

   Nothing is counted here. summary_rows read it all back off the gaps that
   were already raised, so this table cannot say a checkpoint was clean when
   the manifest says otherwise (4.4, 5.4). #}
<section class="section summary" id="summary">

  <h2>Run summary</h2>

  {% if summary_rows %}

    <p class="lede">
      Every checkpoint on the route, in the order it was recorded. Evidence
      counts are the views that produced a usable image; a view whose image is
      missing or will not open is not counted as captured.
    </p>

    <table class="data-table summary-table">
      <colgroup>
        <col class="col-seq">
        <col class="col-name">
        <col class="col-zone">
        <col class="col-status">
        <col class="col-result">
        <col class="col-rgb">
        <col class="col-thermal">
        <col class="col-sensor">
        <col class="col-count">
      </colgroup>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>#</th>
          <th>Checkpoint</th>
          <th>Zone</th>
          <th>Status</th>
          <th>Result</th>
          <th>RGB</th>
          <th>Thermal</th>
          <th>Sensor</th>
          <th>Findings</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for row in summary_rows %}
          {% set point = row.checkpoint %}
          <tr>
            <td class="figure">{{ point.sequence_number | show("-") }}</td>
            <td>
              {{ point.checkpoint_name }}
              <span class="summary-id">{{ point.checkpoint_id }}</span>
            </td>
            <td>{{ point.zone }}</td>
            <td>
              <span class="badge badge-small badge-{{ point.status | status_style }}">
                {{- point.status -}}
              </span>
            </td>
            <td>
              <span class="badge badge-small badge-{{ point.result_status | verdict_style }}">
                {{- point.result_status -}}
              </span>
            </td>
            <td class="figure">{{ row.rgb }}</td>
            <td class="figure">{{ row.thermal }}</td>
            {# The gap types first, then the few words that say what they were
               about. A reader working down this table can match a cell to the
               manifest without opening the checkpoint's own section (4.4). #}
            <td>
              {% if row.sensor_gaps %}
                {% for name in row.sensor_gaps %}
                  <span class="gap-tag">{{ name }}</span>
                {% endfor %}
                <span class="summary-note">{{ row.sensor }}</span>
              {% else %}
                {{ row.sensor }}
              {% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="figure">{{ row.findings }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>

  {% else %}
    <p class="absent-note">No checkpoints were recorded for this run.</p>
  {% endif %}

</section>
